# Goal: Build Wallet-Based Login Module (Signature Authentication)

This plan outlines the architecture for a highly secure, modern, passwordless login system for AgriChain. Users will authenticate exclusively by connecting their MetaMask wallet and signing a unique challenge message (nonce).

## User Review Required

> [!IMPORTANT]
> The cryptographic validation on the backend requires adding standard Ethereum libraries (like `ethers-core`) to recover and verify wallet signatures. I will add `ethers` and `rand` to your Rust backend. You will need to restart the backend server after installation.

## Open Questions

> [!WARNING]
> 1. **Session Persistence**: I will store the JWT securely in `localStorage` on the frontend for this phase, allowing auto-login when the website is refreshed. Is this acceptable, or do you prefer `httpOnly` cookies?
> 2. **Network Checking**: I will implement basic network checking in the frontend to warn users if they aren't on a supported chain, but since the MVP is chain-agnostic for data reading/writing at the moment, is just a warning sufficient?

## Proposed Changes

---

### Backend (Rust + Axum)

The backend will implement the standard SIWE (Sign-In with Ethereum) pattern.

#### [NEW] Dependencies
- `cargo add ethers rand`

#### [NEW] `backend/src/models/nonce.rs`
Define the MongoDB `Nonce` document structure to store temporary nonces tied to wallet addresses with an expiration timestamp.

#### [MODIFY] `backend/src/models/dto.rs`
Add DTOs:
- `LoginRequestDto` `{ wallet_address }`
- `LoginVerifyDto` `{ wallet_address, signature }`
- `LoginRequestResponse` `{ message, nonce }`

#### [NEW] `backend/src/services/nonce_service.rs`
Handles generating a 6-digit random nonce, storing it in the `nonces` MongoDB collection, and verifying/deleting it upon consumption.

#### [NEW] `backend/src/services/signature_service.rs`
Handles the cryptographic recovery of the wallet address from the provided signature and message using `ethers::core::types::Signature`.

#### [MODIFY] `backend/src/controllers/auth.rs`
Add handlers for:
- `login_request`: Generates and returns a nonce.
- `login_verify`: Validates the signature, verifies user existence, issues JWT.
- `get_profile`: Decodes the JWT and returns the full user profile.

#### [MODIFY] `backend/src/routes/auth.rs`
Mount the new `/login/request`, `/login/verify`, and `/profile` routes.

---

### Frontend (React + Vite)

The frontend will handle wallet connectivity and signature generation using `ethers.js`.

#### [NEW] `frontend/src/store/useAuthStore.js`
A Zustand store managing the authentication state (`isAuthenticated`, `user`, `token`), initialized by checking `localStorage`.

#### [NEW] `frontend/src/pages/Login/`
- `index.jsx`: The main Login container with beautiful background gradients and centered card UI.
- `WalletButton.jsx`: Reusable connect/disconnect button.
- `WalletMismatchModal.jsx`: Alert when connected wallet differs from stored JWT wallet.

#### [MODIFY] `frontend/src/App.jsx`
- Add the `<Route path="/login" element={<Login />} />` route.
- Add Auto-Login logic using `useEffect` that calls `/api/auth/profile` with the stored JWT.

#### [MODIFY] `frontend/src/components/layout/Navbar.jsx`
- Update the "Login" button to route to `/login`.
- If authenticated, hide Login/Register buttons and show a "Dashboard" link and profile avatar instead.

## Verification Plan

### Automated Tests
- Run `cargo check` to verify backend compilation with new crypto crates.
- Run `npm run build` to verify frontend compilation.

### Manual Verification
1. Navigate to `/login`.
2. Connect MetaMask wallet.
3. Trigger the signature request; verify MetaMask pop-up displays the correct nonce message.
4. Sign the message and observe the "Login Successful" animation.
5. Verify the frontend stores the JWT and updates the Navbar to show authenticated state.
6. Refresh the page to verify Auto-Login persistence.
